<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Nowadays sound control interfaces typically operate through buttons, sliders, or virtual touch surfaces. However, the impact of these controls on user experience is often overlooked, despite being a critical factor. Volume adjustments and basic sound settings are usually performed through simple mechanical actions, limiting the interaction between the user and the sound.)
/E (Nowadays sound control interfaces typically operate through buttons, sliders, or virtual touch surfaces. However, the impact of these controls on user experience is often overlooked, despite being a critical factor. Volume adjustments and basic sound settings are usually performed through simple mechanical actions, limiting the interaction between the user and the sound.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
